    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Question\n\nIs it by design that mini.files doesn't sync to the nvim default path?\r\n\r\nFor e.g I opened mini.files in `foo/bar/`  and after I do `:cd ..` in neovim  and after doing `:lua Minifiles.reset()`, it doesn't sync with the nvim path, but it syncs with the path that it was opened with.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.files</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is it by design that mini.files doesn't sync to the nvim default path?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For e.g I opened mini.files in <code class=\"notranslate\">foo/bar/</code>  and after I do <code class=\"notranslate\">:cd ..</code> in neovim  and after doing <code class=\"notranslate\">:lua Minifiles.reset()</code>, it doesn't sync with the nvim path, but it syncs with the path that it was opened with.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.files\nQuestion\nIs it by design that mini.files doesn't sync to the nvim default path?\nFor e.g I opened mini.files in foo/bar/  and after I do :cd .. in neovim  and after doing :lua Minifiles.reset(), it doesn't sync with the nvim path, but it syncs with the path that it was opened with.",
    "category": {
