    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2026-09-06T08:22:31Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58370433?u=f27c5d8743e4a42fc8bc9fe3bd6484f6571061cb&v=4",
                "login": "abeldekat",
                "resourcePath": "/abeldekat",
                "url": "https://github.com/abeldekat"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hello @kebiBGit \r\n\r\nThanks for the question!\r\n\r\nThe title mentions `MiniFiles.reset()`. However, that function is not related to synchronization([`:h MiniFiles.reset()`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles.reset)). If you started in \"bar\", `reset` will shrink the explorer to contain only the \"bar\" window, removing all others.\r\n\r\nSynchronization only occurs([`:h MiniFiles.synchronize()`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles.synchronize)) when invoked explicitly or when closing the explorer. The process acts on all directory buffers opened in the current explorer. The underlying current working directory is not relevant here.\r\n\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/kebiBGit/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/kebiBGit\">@kebiBGit</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the question!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The title mentions <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFiles.reset()</code>. However, that function is not related to synchronization(<a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles.reset\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">:h MiniFiles.reset()</code></a>). If you started in \"bar\", <code class=\"notranslate\">reset</code> will shrink the explorer to contain only the \"bar\" window, removing all others.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Synchronization only occurs(<a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles.synchronize\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">:h MiniFiles.synchronize()</code></a>) when invoked explicitly or when closing the explorer. The process acts on all directory buffers opened in the current explorer. The underlying current working directory is not relevant here.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Hello @kebiBGit\nThanks for the question!\nThe title mentions MiniFiles.reset(). However, that function is not related to synchronization(:h MiniFiles.reset()). If you started in \"bar\", reset will shrink the explorer to contain only the \"bar\" window, removing all others.\nSynchronization only occurs(:h MiniFiles.synchronize()) when invoked explicitly or when closing the explorer. The process acts on all directory buffers opened in the current explorer. The underlying current working directory is not relevant here.",
