                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "To add to this (correct) answer, [`reset()` acts based on what's called an \"anchor directory\"](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/ee23d71c02440668cbca5b0cd8640d79d5bc250b/doc/mini-files.txt#L785-L791), i.e. the [one used for opening the explorer](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/ee23d71c02440668cbca5b0cd8640d79d5bc250b/doc/mini-files.txt#L747-L751). To make `:cd` have effect on `reset()`, close the current explorer and start a new one without arguments (it will use current directory as an anchor by default).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">To add to this (correct) answer, <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/ee23d71c02440668cbca5b0cd8640d79d5bc250b/doc/mini-files.txt#L785-L791\"><code class=\"notranslate\">reset()</code> acts based on what's called an \"anchor directory\"</a>, i.e. the <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/ee23d71c02440668cbca5b0cd8640d79d5bc250b/doc/mini-files.txt#L747-L751\">one used for opening the explorer</a>. To make <code class=\"notranslate\">:cd</code> have effect on <code class=\"notranslate\">reset()</code>, close the current explorer and start a new one without arguments (it will use current directory as an anchor by default).</p>",
                    "bodyText": "To add to this (correct) answer, reset() acts based on what's called an \"anchor directory\", i.e. the one used for opening the explorer. To make :cd have effect on reset(), close the current explorer and start a new one without arguments (it will use current directory as an anchor by default).",
